  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1029 PM CDT Fri May 15 2026\n\nThe warming trend continues into early next week with temperatures \npeaking into the low-90s on Monday. Our next chance of rain is still \non track for the mid-week period as a large trough with a cold front \ntakes shape to our west. Late Tuesday and into Wednesday has the \nhighest rain chances. Probability of exceeding 0.50\" through \nWednesday has come up to around 70-80% with the western half of \nMiddle TN being favored for higher amounts with 40-50% probability of\ngetting above one inch.\n\nSeasonable temperatures will return late week as the front tracks \nsouth late Wednesday into Thursday. Rain looks to linger into \nThursday behind the front, but drier air will filter from the north \nto end the week and temperatures will slowly start to warm back \nup again.",
